SUMMARY: FRIDAY NIGHT LIVE @ COLLECTIVE ARTS
DESCRIPTION:Kick off your weekend with a night of laughs at Collective Ar
 ts Toronto Friday\, May 1st.\n\n\nJoin us for a night of live comedy\, gr
 eat drinks\, and good company in the heart of Toronto. Whether you're com
 ing out with friends\, planning a date night\, or just looking for someth
 ing fun to do on a Friday\, this is the perfect way to start the weekend.
 \n\n\nCome early\, grab a drink\, and settle in for an evening of live en
 tertainment in a creative\, laid-back atmosphere. Our kitchen is open fro
 m 5pm\, serving up a great selection of authentic Mexican dishes.\n\n\nEv
 ent Details:\n\nFriday\, May 1\, 2026\n\nCollective Arts Toronto (lower l
 evel venue)\n\n777 Dundas Street West\n\n19+ event\n\nDoors 7pm\n\nShow 8
 pm\n\nTickets: $25 + taxes & fees (includes your first beverage)\n\n\nPre
 sented by BHG Entertainment\n\n\n\nHeadliner\n\nRob Pue\n\nWhat's in the 
 Hotdogs (**YouTube 2026)\, Puegilist (2016)\n\nJust For Laughs\, MTV's Pu
 nk'd\n\n\nFeaturing\n\nFaris Hytiaa\n\nHomesick (**2026 Juno Nominee)\, S
 end Help (2023)\n\nThe New Wave of Stand-Up (CBC)\, Roast Battle Canada (
 CTV Comedy)\n\nLexa Graham\n\nCBC Gem\, Dirty Science\n\n\nHosted by\n\nJ
 eff Paul\n\nDelightfully Dark (2020)\n\nJust For Laughs\, Icebreakers Com
 edy
CATEGORIES:Comedy,Collective-Arts-Toronto
