SUMMARY: New Music for Old Hands Concert Series: Louise Campbell (joining
  us virtually from Montreal)
DESCRIPTION:Matinee concert series at Labdara Lithuanian Nursing Home. Ea
 ch concert in this series will premiere a composition performed by the La
 bdara bell choir and Laura Gillis (conductor/pianist). Each composer will
  give a talk and share music with the residents and audience members\, fo
 llowed by a casual social mixer.\n\n2:00pm start time. Free Admission. Re
 serve your spot at Eventbrite. Limited seating available.\n\nMay 16: Loui
 se Campbell (joining us virtually from Montreal)\n\nLouise will join us f
 rom Montreal (via Zoom) to talk about growing up in a choir and her exper
 ience with creating participatory music with community members. She will 
 share her choral piece State of Sea\, will share an excerpt from Music Di
 aries which was co-created with Anne McIsaac\, a woman who has Parkinson'
 s Disease\, and will lead an interactive activity in which audience membe
 rs will respond to live music played by Louise on the clarinet. The Labda
 ra bell choir and Laura Gillis (conductor/pianist) will premiere Louise's
  piece\, Let Ring.\n\nMay 30: Lieke van der Voort (joining us virtually f
 rom Germany)\n\nJune 13: Alex Eddington\n\nJune 20: Martin van de Ven\n\n
 www.facebook.com/NewMusicForOldHands http://www.facebook.com/NewMusicForO
 ldHands
CATEGORIES:Music,Concert,#poweredbyTAC,#BringingTheArtsToLife
